ked singularity interiors: decay and the role of blue-shift"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"arXiv","value":"[66] Jaydeep Singh. High regularity waves on self-similar naked singularity interiors: decay and the role of blue-shift, 2024."}]},{"reference":{"texkey":"singhphdtheis","label":"67","publication_info":{"year":2025},"misc":["Jaydeep Singh. Regimes of (in-)stability for self-similar naked singularities. PhD thesis"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"arXiv","value":"[67] Jaydeep Singh. Regimes of (in-)stability for self-similar naked singularities. PhD thesis, 2025."}]},{"reference":{"texkey":"zhenglinear","label":"68","misc":["Jaydeep Singh and Weihao Zheng. Violation of the weak cosmic censorship conjecture in the spherical gravitational collapse of a scalar field II: linearized stability"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"arXiv","value":"[68] Jaydeep Singh and Weihao Zheng. Violation of the weak cosmic censorship conjecture in the spherical gravitational collapse of a scalar field II: linearized stability."}]},{"reference":{"texkey":"Wald1984","label":"69","publication_info":{"year":1984},"misc":["General Relativity. University of Chicago Press, Chicago"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Wald, Robert M."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"arXiv","value":"[69] Robert M. Wald. General Relativity. University of Chicago Press, Chicago, 1984."}]},{"reference":{"texkey":"weissenbacher2025mode","arxiv_eprint":"2503.02632","label":"70","publication_info":{"year":2025},"misc":["Max Weissenbacher, Herbert Koch, and Roland Donninger. Mode stability of blow-up for wave maps in the absence of symmetry. arXiv preprint"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"arXiv","value":"[70] Max Weissenbacher, Herbert Koch, and Roland Donninger. Mode stability of blow-up for wave maps in the absence of symmetry. arXiv preprint arXiv:2503.02632, 2025."}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2896882"}},{"reference":{"texkey":"zhengcharged","label":"71","misc":["Weihao Zheng. Charged naked singularities with non-decaying Maxwell field for the Einstein-Maxwell-charged scalar field equations. In preparation"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"arXiv","value":"[71] Weihao Zheng. Charged naked singularities with non-decaying Maxwell field for the Einstein–Maxwell-charged scalar field equations. In preparation."}]}],"number_of_pages":54,"referenced_authors_bais":["R.Donninger.2","A.G.Wasserman.3","P.Biernat.1","P.Bizon.1","P.Breitenlohner.1","R.Penrose.1","D.Maison.1","O.Costin.1","D.Hilditch.1","M.McNulty.1","M.Weissenbacher.2","Xiao.Mi.Xia.1","P.N.Chen.1","M.W.Choptuik.1","D.Wallauch.1","I.Glogic.1","C.Gundlach.1","J.Li.29","J.Liu.40","R.Donninger.5","H.Koch.1","M.Ostermann.1","X.P.Zhu.1","Min.Huang.1","Demetrios.Christodoulou.1","B.Schorkhuber.1"],"inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Math and Math Physics","source":"arxiv"}],"preprint_date":"2026-05-15","author_count":1,"first_author":{"emails":["wz344@math.rutgers.edu"],"full_name":"Zheng, Weihao","last_name":"Zheng","first_name":"Weihao","recid":1975757},"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"54 pages"}],"control_number":3156701,"earliest_date":"2026-05-15","document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Zheng:2026zrt"],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"This is the first part of a series of papers proving the nonlinear stability of a one-parameter family of continuously self-similar $C^{1,α}$ naked singularity solutions, with $0<α\\ll1$, to the spherically symmetric Einstein-scalar field equations. The stability holds for initial perturbations lying in a small open neighborhood of the data generating these naked singularity solutions, measured in a localized Hölder topology. These continuously self-similar naked singularity spacetimes were previously constructed by Christodoulou [D. Christodoulou, Examples of naked singularity formation in the gravitational collapse of a scalar field, Ann. of Math. 140 (1994), 607--653], who also proved their instability to black hole formation under sufficiently rough perturbations [D. Christodoulou, The instability of naked singularities in the gravitational collapse of a scalar field, Ann. of Math. 149 (1999), 183--217], thereby verifying weak cosmic censorship within a rough functional framework. In complete contrast, in this paper, we obtain the first nonlinear stability of these naked singularity spacetimes under general perturbations of the same regularity as the background. We rely on the linearized stability result established in the companion paper [J. Singh and W. Zheng, Nonlinear stability of continuously self-similar naked singularities for the Einstein--scalar field equations II: linearized stability]. Our result underscores the decisive role of the functional framework in formulating the Weak Cosmic Censorship conjecture.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Nonlinear stability of continuously self-similar naked singularities for the Einstein-scalar field equations I: main results"}],"facet_author_name":["1975757_W. Zheng"],"license":[{"license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:3156701","updated":"2026-05-19T04:08:42.047009"},"curated":false,"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc","math-ph","math.AP","math.MP"],"value":"2605.16235"}]},"created":"2026-05-18T04:08:46.426741+00:00","id":"3156701","updated":"2026-05-19T04:08:42.047009+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3156701?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3156701?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3156701?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3156701?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3156701?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3156701?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A3156701"}},{"metadata":{"citation_count":16,"citation_count_without_self_citations":11,"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Mathematics, Asutosh College, Kolkata 700 026, India"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"rudra, prabir","full_name":"Rudra, Prabir","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1073210"},"last_name":"Rudra","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"P.Rudra.1"}],"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/1475137"},"value":"Asutosh Coll., Kolkata"}],"signature_block":"RADRp","first_name":"Prabir","uuid":"567f090c-e106-46f9-8350-690ea57f28fa","recid":1073210}],"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"31","artid":"2250095","year":2022,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1613976"},"journal_issue":"13","journal_title":"Int.J.Mod.Phys.D"}],"citeable":true,"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","keywords":[{"source":"author","value":"Gravitational collapse"},{"source":"author","value":"modified gravity theory"},{"source":"author","value":"Modified gravity"},{"source":"author","value":"gravitational collapse"},{"source":"author","value":"black hole"},{"source":"author","value":"naked singularity"},{"source":"author","value":"Vaidya spacetime"},{"source":"author","value":"Vaidya"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"gravitation: collapse"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"space-time: time dependence"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"coupling: nonminimal"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"black hole: collapse"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"matter: coupling"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"gravitation: model"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"coupling: minimal"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"space-time: Vaidya"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"star: massive"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"singularity"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"curvatur